diagnosis_text:
There is no fault in this topology. A systematic end-to-end investigation of every layer in PC3's forwarding path found the network to be fully operational. At Layer 2, PC3's port on aswb2 (eth0) is correctly configured with PVID 10 / egress-untagged, placing it in the 10.3.0.0/24 VLAN. Both uplink ports (eth1 to dswb1, eth2 to dswb2) carry VLANs 10, 20, 30, and 99 with no errors or drops. At Layer 3, PC3's ARP for its gateway (10.3.0.1) was answered immediately by dswb1 (which holds the VRRP/VIP for VLAN 10). ICMP tests from PC3 reached pc2 in Office A (10.1.0.101, 0% loss, TTL=61 confirming 3 router hops), srv1 in Office B VLAN 30 (10.5.0.4, 0% loss), and r1 (10.0.0.33, 0% loss). Bidirectional tests from pc1 and pc2 back to PC3 also succeeded. The OSPF control plane on both dswb1 and dswb2 shows all three expected adjacencies (peer switch + csw1 + csw2) in Full state, with complete routing tables including the 0.0.0.0/0 default route. The helpdesk ticket's claim that PC3 has been "completely isolated" since the maintenance window is not supported by any live evidence. No device or link needs to be restarted; the reported symptom does not exist in the current lab state.
=== END ===